  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> denote the number that turns up when a fair die is rolled. If the probability that the system of equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>has unique solution is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the sum of value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;and all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
